{"metadata":{"title":"Localization","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"TUIkit"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Localization","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Build multilingual terminal applications with TUIkit’s comprehensive internationalization system.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/localization"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppLifecycle","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Architecture"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit provides built-in support for 5 languages: English, German, French, Italian, and Spanish. All framework strings use a type-safe, dot-notation based localization system with persistent language preferences and automatic fallback chains."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Key-Features","level":3,"text":"Key Features","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Type-safe keys"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Compile-time verified ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizationKey"},{"text":" enums with IDE autocomplete","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"5 languages built-in"}]},{"type":"text","text":": EN, DE, FR, IT, ES with complete translations"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Persistent storage"}],"type":"strong"},{"tex